<p>The Trump administration is preparing to close the U.S. military-run Civil-Military Coordination Centre in Israel, which monitors the Israel-Hamas ceasefire and works to improve aid flows to Palestinians, seven diplomats familiar with its operations told Reuters. The U.S.-led Board of Peace disputed the report. Diplomats told Reuters the CMCC’s aid and monitoring duties would shift to a U.S.-commanded International Stabilisation Force intended for Gaza; they said the transfer would effectively end the CMCC’s role. Diplomats cited by Reuters said the ceasefire framework has faced repeated Israeli attacks since the October truce, Hamas’ refusal to disarm, Israeli territorial advances in Gaza and Hamas control in areas it holds.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7gaRn3QrbNPqwQ-PEasUfe2xMOjWB1yUW0hgecWpAw-SRSeIXQVW9r7cqzpV_VomyMYhkic1zJGeNE-Tx39oJFnLT_dTx3tjaJsQFJsXk9q-' alt='U.S. and Israeli soldiers convene at the Civil Military Coordination Centre, the U.S.-led centre overseeing the implementation of President Donald Trump&#x27;s plan to end the war in Gaza, in Kiryat Gat, southern Israel, November 17, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Limited enforcement: Diplomats told Reuters the CMCC lacked authority to enforce the ceasefire, making it unclear whether any successor could compel compliance.</li><li>Allied concerns: Diplomats said the move could unsettle U.S. allies that President Trump encouraged to send personnel to the CMCC and commit money to his Gaza rebuilding plan.</li><li>Rebuilding stalled: Diplomats said the Gaza reconstruction plan is largely on hold after the United States launched a joint war with Israel against Iran.</li><li>Command location: Israeli media identified the CMCC as operating in Kiryat Gat, southern Israel, near Gaza.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Diplomats familiar with CMCC operations: The diplomats spoke on condition of anonymity because they were not authorised to discuss the mission publicly, Reuters reported. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996844/us-to-close-its-flagship-gaza-mission'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>U.S. officials: U.S. officials privately described the planned transfer as an overhaul rather than a closure, according to diplomats cited by Reuters. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457926/us-to-close-its-flagship-gaza-mission-as-trump-plan-stalls'>Aaj News</a>)</li><li>Board of Peace: The U.S.-led board said in an X post that “Any claim that the CMCC is closing is wrong” and described the centre as the main hub for stabilisation work, ceasefire implementation monitoring and aid facilitation. (<a href='https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/05/01/board-of-peace-denies-claims-us-run-ceasefire-monitoring-centre-in-gaza-shutting-down/'>The National</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-to-close-its-flagship-gaza-mission-as-donald-trump-plan-stalls/article70930743.ece'>U.S. to close its flagship Gaza mission as Donald Trump plan stalls</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1996844/us-to-close-its-flagship-gaza-mission'>US to ‘close its flagship Gaza mission’</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-palestine-war-us-military-run-mission-for-gaza-aid-set-to-close-soon-report-11437431#publisher=newsstand'>US Military-Run Mission For Gaza Aid Set To Close Soon: Report</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/uae-says-iran-cannot-be-trusted-over-hormuz-peace-efforts-an-impasse-2026-05-01/'>Reuters says that the U.S. was planning to close the Civil-Military Coordination Center. The Board of Peace denies such reports.</a> - reuters.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ynetnews.com/article/ryhhphfrzg'>US to close flagship Gaza mission as Hamas tightens grip and Trump plan stalls, report says</a> - ynetnews.com</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457926/us-to-close-its-flagship-gaza-mission-as-trump-plan-stal